# M16: Save As in the file dialog. It starts with the document's name selected and the folder it is in; changing the type swaps the
# extension; a name that is there asks before it is replaced (No is the default, then Yes saves); New folder makes a folder and
# selects it; a read-only file is refused; Esc leaves. New folder comes before the first save, so no box covers the date of a file this
# run has just written (DOS stamps those with the real time, which the DOS run replaces with the host's before it compares).
@dialog
@dir QUILL
@place Quill C:\QUILL
@cwd C:\DOCS
@dir DOCS\LETTERS
@copy letter.qld DOCS\
@copy letter.rtf DOCS\
@copy plain.qld DOCS\
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.QLD 2026-11-24 18:45
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.RTF 2026-11-02 09:05
@stamp DOCS\PLAIN.QLD 2026-03-14 12:00
@readonly DOCS\PLAIN.QLD
@open C:\DOCS\LETTER.QLD
f10 down down down enter      # File > Save As...: LETTER.QLD, selected
altt down                     # Save as type: Rich Text Format; the name becomes LETTER.RTF
enter                         # LETTER.RTF is there: Do you want to replace it?
enter                         # No is the default: back to the dialog
altf d r a f t s enter        # New folder DRAFTS: made and selected
altn n e w enter              # NEW.RTF: saved
f10 down down down enter      # File > Save As... again: NEW.RTF is in the list now
l e t t e r period r t f enter y   # LETTER.RTF again: Yes replaces it
f10 down down down enter
altn p l a i n period q l d enter   # PLAIN.QLD is read-only
enter                         # OK
esc                           # Cancel
